exports[`golden — SKILL.md > default schema 1`] = `
"# My Design System — Design System Skill

This file tells an AI agent how to build UI that conforms to this design system.
The normative source of truth is \`design-spec.schema.json\`; \`DESIGN.md\` carries the human rationale.

## Golden rule

Always reference design tokens. Never hard-code raw values (hex, px, \`Color(0xFF…)\`).
Raw values are *drift* and are auto-rewritten to the nearest token by \`design-spec fix\` and the CI Drift-Janitor.

## Getting context efficiently

Run \`design-spec serve\` to expose this schema over MCP. Request only the slice you need:
- \`get_component_tokens("Button")\` — tokens for one component.
- \`get_layout_system()\` — grid, spacing, container, breakpoints.
- \`get_semantic_colors()\` — semantic color roles (not the raw palette).

## Frameworks

### React + Tailwind

- Reference tokens via Tailwind utilities, never inline hex. e.g. \`className="text-primary rounded-md"\`.
- Token names map 1:1 to \`tailwind.config.js\` theme keys generated from the schema.
- Never write \`text-[#...]\` arbitrary values — that is drift and will be auto-fixed.

## Components

#### Button
Primary action trigger. The most-referenced component in any UI.
- Anatomy: root › label › icon › spinner
- Variants: primary, secondary, ghost, destructive · Sizes: sm, md, lg · States: default, hover, active, disabled, loading
- Props:
  - \`variant\`: enum(primary|secondary|ghost|destructive)
  - \`size\`: enum(sm|md|lg)
  - \`disabled\`: boolean
  - \`loading\`: boolean
  - \`label\`: string (required) — Button text

#### Input
Single-line text field with label, helper text, and error message.
- Anatomy: root › label › field › helper › error
- Variants: default · Sizes: md · States: default, focus, error, disabled
- Props:
  - \`type\`: enum(text|password|search)
  - \`placeholder\`: string
  - \`disabled\`: boolean
  - \`error\`: string — Error message; renders the error state

#### Card
Elevated container for grouped content. Padding grows on larger viewports.
- Anatomy: root › header › body › footer
- Variants: default, interactive, outlined · Sizes: — · States: default, hover
- Props:
  - \`variant\`: enum(default|interactive|outlined)

#### Badge
Compact status or category label.
- Anatomy: root › label
- Variants: neutral, success, warning, error, info · Sizes: sm, md · States: default
- Props:
  - \`variant\`: enum(neutral|success|warning|error|info)

#### Alert
Inline contextual feedback banner. Color, border, and icon follow the status.
- Anatomy: root › icon › title › description › close
- Variants: info, success, warning, error · Sizes: — · States: default
- Props:
  - \`variant\`: enum(info|success|warning|error)
  - \`iconPlacement\`: enum(leading|trailing|none) — Where the status icon sits
  - \`content\`: enum(title-message|message) — Title + message, or message only
  - \`dismissible\`: boolean

#### Checkbox
Binary or indeterminate selection control with optional label.
- Anatomy: root › box › check › label
- Variants: default · Sizes: md · States: unchecked, checked, indeterminate, disabled
- Props:
  - \`checked\`: boolean
  - \`indeterminate\`: boolean
  - \`label\`: string

#### Tooltip
Small floating label revealed on hover or focus.
- Anatomy: root › arrow › label
- Variants: default · Sizes: — · States: default
- Props:
  - \`placement\`: enum(top|right|bottom|left)
  - \`label\`: string (required)

#### Dropdown
Select trigger that opens a list of options.
- Anatomy: trigger › value › icon › menu › option
- Variants: default · Sizes: sm, md, lg · States: default, open, disabled
- Props:
  - \`placeholder\`: string
  - \`searchable\`: boolean
  - \`disabled\`: boolean

#### Radio
Single-choice control within a group.
- Anatomy: root › control › dot › label
- Variants: default · Sizes: md · States: unchecked, checked, disabled
- Props:
  - \`checked\`: boolean
  - \`label\`: string
  - \`name\`: string — Group name

#### Navbar
Top navigation bar with brand, links, and actions. Links collapse behind a menu toggle on small screens.
- Anatomy: root › brand › links › actions › menu-toggle
- Variants: default · Sizes: — · States: default, menu-open
- Props:
  - \`sticky\`: boolean
  - \`brand\`: string — Brand name or logo alt text
- Responsive (mobile-first; base applies until the breakpoint):
  - ≥768px (md): paddingX: {spacing.lg} — Links render inline and the menu toggle is hidden; below md the links collapse behind the toggle.

#### Sidebar
Vertical navigation. One-level (flat) or multilevel (nested, collapsible groups). Collapses to an icon rail on small screens.
- Anatomy: root › item › group › sub-item › collapse-toggle
- Variants: one-level, multilevel · Sizes: — · States: default, collapsed
- Props:
  - \`collapsed\`: boolean
  - \`collapsible\`: boolean — Show the collapse toggle
- Responsive (mobile-first; base applies until the breakpoint):
  - ≥768px (md): — — Expanded rail with labels; below md the sidebar collapses to an icon rail.

#### Tabs
Switches between related panels in place. Line, pill, or contained; horizontal or vertical.
- Anatomy: root › tablist › tab › indicator › panel
- Variants: line, pill, contained · Sizes: — · States: default, hover, selected, disabled
- Props:
  - \`variant\`: enum(line|pill|contained)
  - \`orientation\`: enum(horizontal|vertical)
  - \`children\`: slot — Tab list and panels
- Responsive (mobile-first; base applies until the breakpoint):
  - ≥768px (md): — — Vertical orientation is honored; below md tabs are one horizontal row that scrolls.

#### Breadcrumbs
Hierarchical trail to the current page, with a tokenized separator.
- Anatomy: root › item › separator › current
- Variants: default · Sizes: — · States: default, hover
- Props:
  - \`separator\`: enum(chevron|slash|dot)
- Responsive (mobile-first; base applies until the breakpoint):
  - ≥768px (md): — — Full trail; below md the middle crumbs collapse to an ellipsis.

#### Pagination
Numbered page links with previous / next controls.
- Anatomy: root › prev › item › ellipsis › next
- Variants: default · Sizes: sm, md · States: default, hover, current, disabled
- Props:
  - \`page\`: number — Current page (1-based)
  - \`pageCount\`: number
  - \`showPrevNext\`: boolean
- Responsive (mobile-first; base applies until the breakpoint):
  - ≥768px (md): — — Numbered pages; below md only previous / next with "Page x of y".

#### Accordion
Stacked disclosure sections. Single or multiple open; height animates unless reduced motion is set.
- Anatomy: root › item › trigger › icon › content
- Variants: default · Sizes: — · States: collapsed, expanded, disabled
- Props:
  - \`type\`: enum(single|multiple) — How many sections may be open at once
  - \`children\`: slot — Accordion items

#### Progress
Progress bar. Determinate shows a value; indeterminate shows ongoing work with no known end.
- Anatomy: root › track › fill › label
- Variants: determinate, indeterminate · Sizes: sm, md · States: default, complete
- Props:
  - \`value\`: number
  - \`max\`: number
  - \`label\`: string — Accessible name

#### EmptyState
Placeholder for a view with no content yet: icon, title, description, and a next action.
- Anatomy: root › icon › title › description › action
- Variants: default · Sizes: — · States: default
- Props:
  - \`title\`: string
  - \`description\`: string
  - \`actionLabel\`: string
- Responsive (mobile-first; base applies until the breakpoint):
  - ≥768px (md): padding: {spacing.2xl}

#### ErrorState
Full-view error: not found (404), server error (500), or no permission (403), with a recovery action.
- Anatomy: root › code › icon › title › description › action
- Variants: not-found, server-error, forbidden · Sizes: — · States: default
- Props:
  - \`variant\`: enum(not-found|server-error|forbidden)
  - \`actionLabel\`: string
- Responsive (mobile-first; base applies until the breakpoint):
  - ≥768px (md): padding: {spacing.2xl}

#### Table
Tabular data with sortable headers, row selection, and a pagination slot. Rows stack into cards on small screens.
- Anatomy: root › header › header-cell › sort-icon › row › cell › select › pagination
- Variants: default · Sizes: — · States: default, row-hover, row-selected, sorted
- Props:
  - \`sortable\`: boolean
  - \`selectable\`: boolean
  - \`pagination\`: slot — Pagination under the table
- Responsive (mobile-first; base applies until the breakpoint):
  - ≥768px (md): — — Full table; below md each row stacks into a label / value card.

#### Drawer
Panel that slides in from the left, right, or bottom over an overlay. Becomes a bottom sheet on small screens.
- Anatomy: overlay › root › header › title › close › body › footer
- Variants: default · Sizes: sm, md, lg · States: open, closed
- Props:
  - \`side\`: enum(left|right|bottom)
  - \`open\`: boolean
  - \`title\`: string
  - \`children\`: slot — Drawer body
- Responsive (mobile-first; base applies until the breakpoint):
  - ≥768px (md): — — Side panel from the chosen edge; below md it renders as a bottom sheet.
"
`;

exports[`golden — SKILL.md > renders per-component responsive snippets 1`] = `
"# Responsive Fixture — Design System Skill

This file tells an AI agent how to build UI that conforms to this design system.
The normative source of truth is \`design-spec.schema.json\`; \`DESIGN.md\` carries the human rationale.

## Golden rule

Always reference design tokens. Never hard-code raw values (hex, px, \`Color(0xFF…)\`).
Raw values are *drift* and are auto-rewritten to the nearest token by \`design-spec fix\` and the CI Drift-Janitor.

## Getting context efficiently

Run \`design-spec serve\` to expose this schema over MCP. Request only the slice you need:
- \`get_component_tokens("Button")\` — tokens for one component.
- \`get_layout_system()\` — grid, spacing, container, breakpoints.
- \`get_semantic_colors()\` — semantic color roles (not the raw palette).

## Frameworks

### React + Tailwind

- Reference tokens via Tailwind utilities, never inline hex. e.g. \`className="text-primary rounded-md"\`.
- Token names map 1:1 to \`tailwind.config.js\` theme keys generated from the schema.
- Never write \`text-[#...]\` arbitrary values — that is drift and will be auto-fixed.

## Components

#### Button
A clickable action trigger. Primary drives the single most important action per view.
- Anatomy: root › label › icon › spinner
- Variants: primary, secondary · Sizes: sm, md, lg · States: default, hover, focus, disabled, loading
- Props:
  - \`variant\`: enum(primary|secondary)
  - \`size\`: enum(sm|md|lg)
  - \`disabled\`: boolean
  - \`loading\`: boolean
  - \`children\`: slot — Button label content.
- Responsive (mobile-first; base applies until the breakpoint):
  - ≥768px (tablet): paddingX: {spacing.lg} — comfortable padding
  - ≥1024px (desktop): paddingX: {spacing.xl}; paddingY: {spacing.md} — wider hit target

#### Input
A single-line text field with label, helper text, and error states.
- Anatomy: root › label › field › helper
- Variants: default · Sizes: md · States: default, focus, disabled, error
- Props:
  - \`label\`: string
  - \`placeholder\`: string
  - \`disabled\`: boolean
  - \`error\`: string — Error message; switches the field to its error state.
"
`;

